1
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:20,667
Until the early twelve hundreds, humanity
did not know that dragons existed.

2
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,208
The seas had names.
The kingdoms had borders.

3
00:00:47,625 --> 00:00:50,208
Beyond them lay islands
no one had reached,

4
00:00:50,292 --> 00:00:52,625
and things no one had thought to fear.

5
00:00:56,333 --> 00:01:05,875
Tara. Scrapper. Verdor.
The Citadel Sea and the Proxy Sea.

6
00:01:06,667 --> 00:01:11,000
Seven kingdoms, and undiscovered
islands beyond the familiar shores.

7
00:01:20,292 --> 00:01:24,000
By the fourteen hundreds,
dragons were part of our lives.

8
00:01:24,292 --> 00:01:26,375
So were the people who rode them.

9
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,417
This is where our story begins.

10
00:02:01,375 --> 00:02:03,167
It started a moment ago.

11
00:02:03,292 --> 00:02:04,833
Has anyone touched it?

12
00:02:04,917 --> 00:02:06,667
No, Your Majesty.

13
00:02:06,792 --> 00:02:08,167
Then let it finish.

14
00:02:44,375 --> 00:02:45,625
Look at it.

15
00:02:50,167 --> 00:02:51,875
My pretty little weapon

16
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:05,542
Is it out?

17
00:03:06,583 --> 00:03:07,750
Come slowly.

18
00:03:12,583 --> 00:03:13,542
It's gold.

19
00:03:13,625 --> 00:03:14,917
I can see that.

20
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,250
I mean all of it.

21
00:03:23,667 --> 00:03:25,625
Wait. Let it settle.

22
00:03:26,375 --> 00:03:28,375
How long has it been trying?

23
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:31,458
Long enough. It needs rest now.

24
00:03:38,875 --> 00:03:39,792
There.

25
00:03:39,875 --> 00:03:40,875
Yes.

26
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,375
Does it have a name?

27
00:03:43,500 --> 00:03:44,458
Not yet.

28
00:03:44,542 --> 00:03:46,042
Don't let him choose it.

29
00:03:48,875 --> 00:03:50,417
I hadn't offered.

30
00:03:51,583 --> 00:03:53,792
Then you may both leave it in peace.

31
00:03:57,500 --> 00:03:58,958
We're going flying.

32
00:03:59,042 --> 00:03:59,917
Together?

33
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:00,792
Yes.

34
00:04:00,875 --> 00:04:02,833
Stay within reach of the island.

35
00:04:02,917 --> 00:04:04,000
We will.

36
00:04:39,083 --> 00:04:40,625
Leaf. Here.

37
00:04:43,792 --> 00:04:44,792
Finished?

38
00:04:44,875 --> 00:04:45,667
Nearly.

39
00:04:45,750 --> 00:04:48,042
That was nearly when I asked before.

40
00:04:48,125 --> 00:04:49,417
You asked once.

41
00:04:54,292 --> 00:04:55,458
The field's clear.

42
00:05:11,083 --> 00:05:12,833
Stay clear when he lifts.

43
00:05:12,958 --> 00:05:13,958
I remember.

44
00:05:14,042 --> 00:05:16,208
Leaf doesn't always remember.

45
00:05:20,708 --> 00:05:21,958
We'll go first.

46
00:06:04,792 --> 00:06:06,708
You could have warned the grass.

47
00:06:29,583 --> 00:06:31,125
Everything secure?

48
00:06:31,333 --> 00:06:32,250
Yes.

49
00:06:32,333 --> 00:06:33,417
All right.

50
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:12,000
You're going to be queen when I'm gone.
Least I think that's how that works.

51
00:07:12,083 --> 00:07:13,500
You good with that?

52
00:07:18,292 --> 00:07:19,583
Yeah, you're good.

53
00:07:32,083 --> 00:07:33,917
Why couldn't I get a Bashion?

54
00:07:35,208 --> 00:07:36,500
You have Leaf.

55
00:07:36,667 --> 00:07:38,083
I know I have Leaf.

56
00:07:38,208 --> 00:07:40,625
Then don't ask like he isn't right here.

57
00:07:44,292 --> 00:07:45,917
I didn't mean it like that.

58
00:07:48,083 --> 00:07:51,208
Nightwings are faster. More versatile.

59
00:07:51,292 --> 00:07:52,417
And Bashions?

60
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:53,917
Better for war.

61
00:07:57,333 --> 00:08:01,458
I was thinking about being able
to move the ground every time I leave.

62
00:08:01,542 --> 00:08:03,708
Someone has to mend it afterward.

63
00:08:03,792 --> 00:08:04,750
Not you.

64
00:08:04,833 --> 00:08:06,000
That's true.

65
00:08:14,417 --> 00:08:15,542
Don't start.

66
00:08:24,833 --> 00:08:25,833
Leaf.

67
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:34,792
That's enough.

68
00:08:40,208 --> 00:08:42,000
He put his head in his mouth.

69
00:08:42,083 --> 00:08:43,167
I saw.

70
00:08:43,250 --> 00:08:44,417
His whole head.

71
00:08:44,500 --> 00:08:45,875
Leaf saw too.

72
00:08:49,708 --> 00:08:52,000
You're all right. Leave him alone.

73
00:08:57,417 --> 00:08:58,792
Still want one?

74
00:08:58,875 --> 00:08:59,875
Yes.

75
00:09:13,917 --> 00:09:14,917
Abby!

76
00:09:18,417 --> 00:09:20,250
Look at me. Abby!

77
00:09:21,125 --> 00:09:21,917
My arm—

78
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,417
Stay with Leaf. Stay on him.

79
00:09:36,958 --> 00:09:38,458
Can he take you in?

80
00:09:38,875 --> 00:09:39,708
Yes.

81
00:09:39,792 --> 00:09:42,667
Go straight back. I'll be behind you.

82
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:46,417
Home. Come on.

83
00:09:52,958 --> 00:09:54,000
Attack.
